# Nothing here runs: the file no longer ends in .yml, so GitHub does not parse
# it, and every line below is commented out as well. A tag pushed today starts
# nothing at all.
#
# It is kept because the pipeline itself is worth keeping — version agreement,
# six cross-compiled targets, a wheel per target, and a smoke run that drives a
# real Chrome on each platform. None of it has ever executed.
#
# To bring it back:
#
#     cd .github/workflows
#     sed -i 's/^# \?//' release.yml.disabled
#     # then drop this header block and rename:
#     git mv release.yml.disabled release.yml
#
# and re-read the switch-on order above the publish jobs before uncommenting
# those — they are commented a second time, inside this one, on purpose.
#
# name: Release
